    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d837">

                <pb facs="0978" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg884"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to
                            Mavroyeni Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 11th instant, embodying the reply of Tevfik Pasha to mine of
                    May 29 last, regarding the destruction of American property at Harpoot and the
                    conduct of the Turkish authorities in connection therewith.</p>
                <p>I have sent a copy of your note to Minister Terrell at Constantinople with an
                    appropriate instruction.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
